==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|zle-mru|иша́къ}}, {{m|zle-mru|ише́къ}}, attested in 1567 and 1623. Further borrowed from {{der|ru|trk|}} languages, probably from {{der|ru|qwm|-}}. Compare {{cog|tt|ишәк}}, {{cog|ba|ишәк}}, also {{cog|tr|eşek}}, {{cog|crh|eşek}}, {{cog|az|eşşək}}), ultimately from {{der|ru|trk-pro|*eĺčgek}}, which is related to {{cog|tuw-pro|*eyiken}} and {{cog|xgn-pro|*elǰigen}}. {{rfv-etym|ru}}

